{
 "comment": "entity_269st_gap: cash received on one day by two ledgers that carry one PAN, summed over the same population cash_payments_40a3 tests per ledger, reported only where the aggregate reaches the s.269ST(a) limit and no single ledger does. Reaches: a gap row where the names share a word and one where they share none; a PAN whose one ledger already reaches the limit (left to the per-ledger test); an aggregate under the limit; a PAN derived from a GSTIN (an opt-in, into a gap only) and a TAN-shaped GSTIN that gives none; a PAN filled by the engagement's override and one a master already holds (the master wins); a ledger with no PAN left unbound; an entity with one ledger; an excluded ledger and a Duties & Taxes ledger and a round-off ledger that are never parties; a ledger made a party by name outside the party groups; a walk-in sale with only tax and round-off lines (unbound); a Contra and an optional voucher left out.",
